Arara Code: product-configured startup webview before the first workbench render.

Why a patch: extension activation happens after workbench rendering. No extension
API can select the first rendered surface or hide all workbench parts before
activation. Read the extension's existing completion state synchronously through
IExtensionStorageService, using the product's generic startupWebview descriptor.
Keep all workbench chrome hidden while the extension-owned modal is active;
reuse its context gate and native modal, without changing saved user layout.
The extension owns the steps, choices and completion. No timers/reopening tabs.
Window close and quit stay allowed; an unfinished setup reopens on next launch.
Touches: product type, workbench startup, startupWebview and its scoped CSS.

